;; Arbace's addition to Go's package reflect (doc/go/GOI-SPEC.md, "As built: GR9a-c"; the GR9
;; survey, doc/go/GR9-SURVEY.md, §2.2 (A), §3.1, GC65 (a)): the file arbace_named.go, goi's
;; interpreted named types made at run time as runtime types of their own (ArbaceNamed,
;; ArbaceSetLayout, ArbaceSetUnderlying, ArbaceSetMethods). Written in Go after the survey's
;; prototype (X9, its Appendix B) with reflect's own types and helpers (go1.27.1's
;; src/reflect/type.go: structType, uncommonType, newName, resolveReflectName,
;; resolveReflectType, resolveReflectText, toType, fnv1; StructOf's Equal), and converted to Go
;; forms by bin/repr-go read (in a copy of $ARBACE_GOROOT with the file added to src/reflect).
;; Not a package of the program: bin/jrt overlay prints this file and adds it to
;; $GOROOT/src/reflect in the overlay of every build (linux and tamago, amd64 and arm64), beside
;; overlay/go/runtime's files.
(ns go.reflect
  (:require [arbace.go :as go]))

(go/package reflect
  :path "reflect"
  :files ["arbace_named.go"])

(load "reflect/arbace_named")
